0..55 Comment "// Generic equality follows a data type\'s constructors."
56..58 Comment "//"
59..107 Comment "// `Eq.generic(T)` compares values structurally."
108..171 Comment "// The checker judges `Eq.generic(T)` as any other declaration."
172..249 Comment "// `Eq.generic.refl(T)` and `Eq.generic.sym(T)` derive its laws by congruence"
250..324 Comment "// over the constructors of `T`, and rest on the host\'s integer and string"
325..342 Comment "// equality laws."
343..403 Comment "// A model of `Eq` with derived members puts `T` under `==`."
404..406 Comment "//"
407..450 Comment "// Primitive values use their own equality."
451..490 Comment "// Sums compare their constructor side."
491..534 Comment "// Recursive fields use their own equality."
535..582 Comment "// Other data fields use their type\'s equality."
583..658 Comment "// A field of a sum or of `T` itself takes a proof that the derivation does"
659..672 Comment "// not write."
673..675 Comment "//"
676..691 Comment "// - see: #2302"
692..752 Comment "// - see: `../../pathological/data/generic-eq-refused.gandr`"
